From 8dc27e68d9250bfc6d65a21dc59354665ee73c44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patch <patch@local>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 20:30:56 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Relaunch on ESP.restart() and keep RTC memory across it

ESP.restart(), esp_restart() and HalSystem::restart() did nothing (or exited),
so Midad's silent restarts (File Transfer, News, Library, ...) hung the
simulator. They now relaunch the process like a deep-sleep wake does, without
a wake reason.

RTC_NOINIT_ATTR variables go in one section that is saved before the relaunch
and restored before static initialisers run, so the restart target survives
as it does in RTC memory on the device. Deep-sleep wakes keep it too. Linux
only; elsewhere the relaunch still happens but starts cold.

The input and screenshot schedules run on a clock that carries on across a
restart, so one script can span it.
---
